{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06MC", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:69392b937e4ddfc033f031fd28dd170ac7ded924038e9490323d15358ede1ddc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is a useful corollary which tells us that the ``fibres'' of\na DM morphism of algebraic stacks are Deligne-Mumford.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8876ca01d3f3774414740c00fe24b2639df2d390e96dba0d3396dc75ca62bdbe", "unit_id": "tag:06MC:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06MC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$Z$", "MATH_0006": "$Z \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} Z$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-DM}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bd7d72b0ee49e27d5b14cdda6364fb14f18f9ff7350da39d66e1e5d7b6862bb5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a89f40aafdc854c927d26a5e435fca1be36fbba0d119d0c938ccec111e3060a5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a DM morphism of algebraic\nstacks. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> For every DM algebraic stack <MATH_0002> and morphism\n<MATH_0003> there exists a scheme and\na surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism\n<MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every algebraic space <MATH_0005> and morphism\n<MATH_0006> there exists a scheme and\na surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism\n<MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bef44a0ca9ccd503d7241e0f27b575ee2fde2653d1ee0d645a1e0fc9df16da45", "unit_id": "tag:0CIA:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06MC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-separated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-separated-over-separated}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{theorem-DM}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-trivial-implications}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:50cf4f42baf0dd136c73f862670f2949c83c834656fff23abbf3a5bc7b8a9c6a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:acbcda48ab1bb545a5ad9afdd0a7398b11f8a2138b2a211d3ed21db2988813de", "source_text": "Proof of (1). As <MATH_0001> is DM we see that the base change\n<MATH_0002> is DM\nby Lemma <REF_0001>.\nSince <MATH_0003> is DM this implies that\n<MATH_0004> is DM\nby Lemma <REF_0002>. Hence there exists a\nscheme <MATH_0005> and a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism\n<MATH_0006>, see\nTheorem <REF_0003>.\nPart (2) is a special case of (1) since an algebraic space\n(when viewed as an algebraic stack) is DM by\nLemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ce7b30963d047d386f87fda0dbf02b41427d8fa29b0f7cb9d35472275c8b46c2", "unit_id": "tag:0CIA:proof"}
